From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:00:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 077/167] hjviewer: the CM's tab list menu shows its items

U13: the tab list menu (the title bar's down arrow) of the connection
manager window opened as an empty grey box. Each menu row's Obx read
menuHover only after checking tabInfo?.onTabCloseButton, so for tabs
without a close callback (the CM's, port forwarding's) it read no
observable; GetX rejects such an Obx and release builds draw a grey
error box. The condition now reads menuHover.value first, so every
row's Obx reads an observable and the menu lists the tabs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/lib/desktop/widgets/tabbar_widget.dart | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/flutter/lib/desktop/widgets/tabbar_widget.dart b/flutter/lib/desktop/widgets/tabbar_widget.dart
index 70ed806..9972cb4 100644
--- a/flutter/lib/desktop/widgets/tabbar_widget.dart
+++ b/flutter/lib/desktop/widgets/tabbar_widget.dart
@@ -1671,8 +1671,11 @@ class _TabDropDownButtonState extends State<_TabDropDownButton> {
                     ),
                     Obx(
                       () {
-                        if (tabInfo?.onTabCloseButton != null &&
-                            menuHover.value) {
+                        // HJViewer: menuHover first, so that the Obx reads an observable for a
+                        // tab without a close callback too (the CM's, port forwarding's): GetX
+                        // fails an Obx that reads none, and the menu showed an error box
+                        if (menuHover.value &&
+                            tabInfo?.onTabCloseButton != null) {
                           return InkWell(
                               onTap: () {
                                 tabInfo?.onTabCloseButton?.call();
